Data. The MIT licence above covers the code. The data is under its own licences:

- app/data/areas/* (the built premises, roads and relief-centre data) is derived from OpenStreetMap:
  (c) OpenStreetMap contributors, Open Database License (ODbL) 1.0, https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/odbl/1-0/
- The JRC flood depth rasters (app/data/rasters/*.tif) are not in this repository. They are European Commission JRC
  global river flood hazard maps v2.1, CC BY 4.0, https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/ (see
  app/data/rasters/SOURCES.txt).
- The elevation crops (app/data/dem/*.tif) are derived from the Copernicus DEM GLO-30: (c) DLR e.V. 2010-2014 and
  (c) Airbus Defence and Space GmbH 2014-2018 provided under COPERNICUS by the European Union and ESA; all rights
  reserved. Their river levels come from OpenStreetMap rivers, (c) OpenStreetMap contributors, ODbL 1.0 (see
  app/data/dem/SOURCES.txt).
- The flash flood potential files (app/data/indexes/*, and app/data/areas/*/indexes.json) are derived from: ESA
  WorldCover 2021 v200 (CC BY 4.0; ESA WorldCover project 2021 / Contains modified Copernicus Sentinel data (2021)
  processed by ESA WorldCover consortium); ESA WorldCover Sentinel-1 and Sentinel-2 10m Annual Composites accessed on
  4 October 2026 from https://registry.opendata.aws/esa-worldcover-vito-composites (CC BY 4.0); ISRIC SoilGrids 2.0
  (CC BY 4.0, Poggio and others 2021, https://doi.org/10.5194/soil-7-217-2021); WorldPop 2020 constrained 100 m
  (CC BY 4.0, https://doi.org/10.5258/SOTON/WP00660); OpenStreetMap drains, (c) OpenStreetMap contributors, ODbL 1.0;
  and the Copernicus DEM GLO-30 crop above. The method is cited, not copied: Smith (2003) as used by Yassin and
  others (2023), Planning Malaysia 21(2); and, for the weights of the section score, Leeonis and others (2024). See
  app/data/indexes/SOURCES.txt.
